1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,590
What if a third party you trusted at the beginning of a financial

2
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:08,493
workflow became unsafe before the workflow finished?

3
00:00:08,493 --> 00:00:11,396
Would the next operation still be authorized?

4
00:00:11,396 --> 00:00:16,786
Introducing Revoke Line, Team Kappa's contribution to Track Two of the FINOS Fall

5
00:00:16,786 --> 00:00:20,518
2026 Hackathon: Extend and Utilize FINOS Governance as Code.

6
00:00:20,518 --> 00:00:25,494
Our goal is to bring governance into runtime execution, not just deployment.

7
00:00:25,494 --> 00:00:30,884
Revoke Line combines dynamic trust revocation, selective incident containment, and secure recovery when

8
00:00:30,884 --> 00:00:36,275
the policy engine becomes unavailable. This presentation walks through the implemented prototype and

9
00:00:36,275 --> 00:00:37,933
its recorded integration results.

10
00:00:38,533 --> 00:00:41,163
Consider a synthetic Know Your Customer workflow.

11
00:00:41,163 --> 00:00:45,672
A financial institution starts a verification case with an approved external provider.

12
00:00:45,672 --> 00:00:48,678
The case receives a grant at version one.

13
00:00:48,678 --> 00:00:53,562
While the case is running, a security alert changes the provider's trust status.

14
00:00:53,562 --> 00:00:57,695
The provider is revoked, and its authorization version moves to two.

15
00:00:57,695 --> 00:01:00,701
However, the workflow still holds the original grant.

16
00:01:00,701 --> 00:01:04,834
The key question is what happens at the next sensitive operation.

17
00:01:04,834 --> 00:01:08,216
A valid decision made earlier is no longer sufficient.

18
00:01:08,216 --> 00:01:13,100
The authorization must reflect the current trust state at the moment of use.

19
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:17,062
There are two undesirable responses to this incident.

20
00:01:17,062 --> 00:01:22,526
If a workflow relies on cached authorization, it may continue using the compromised

21
00:01:22,526 --> 00:01:27,990
provider. If the institution shuts down every provider, it may also interrupt legitimate

22
00:01:27,990 --> 00:01:31,353
business operations. Revoke Line takes a targeted approach.

23
00:01:31,353 --> 00:01:36,817
It rejects the compromised access while preserving the independent workflow that still has

24
00:01:36,817 --> 00:01:42,281
valid authorization. The first two approaches shown here are conceptual baselines, not measurements

25
00:01:42,281 --> 00:01:47,745
against competing products. The Revoke Line result was observed in a local integration

26
00:01:47,745 --> 00:01:50,267
scenario with two distinct workflow instances.

27
00:01:50,867 --> 00:01:56,564
The contribution builds on the FINOS Governance as Code ecosystem rather than replacing

28
00:01:56,564 --> 00:02:00,947
it. CALM describes the architecture and supports dependency impact analysis.

29
00:02:00,947 --> 00:02:06,644
The Flux Nova engine executes the business process and evaluates a pinned decision

30
00:02:06,644 --> 00:02:12,341
model for runtime authorization. We also map the implementation to selected mitigations in

31
00:02:12,341 --> 00:02:17,600
the AI Governance Framework, and document gaps against selected Common Cloud Controls.

32
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:21,983
CALM and Flux Nova are integrated directly into the prototype.

33
00:02:21,983 --> 00:02:25,927
The other frameworks provide traceability and scoped assurance references.

34
00:02:25,927 --> 00:02:29,433
These references are not claims of official conformance.

35
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:32,809
Here is how the components work together.

36
00:02:32,809 --> 00:02:36,774
A provider incident updates its trust state and grant version.

37
00:02:36,774 --> 00:02:39,550
The CALM graph identifies impacted upstream dependencies.

38
00:02:39,550 --> 00:02:44,705
When a Flux Nova worker requests a sensitive operation, the Revoke Line gateway

39
00:02:44,705 --> 00:02:48,670
checks the case, provider, and grant against the current state.

40
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:52,239
It also evaluates the pinned D M N policy.

41
00:02:52,239 --> 00:02:56,601
Both the local guard and the policy must authorize the request.

42
00:02:56,601 --> 00:02:59,376
The policy cannot override a local denial.

43
00:02:59,376 --> 00:03:04,135
The worker then routes the outcome to automated completion or human review.

44
00:03:04,135 --> 00:03:08,100
Hash-chained audit events support offline verification of the recorded decisions.

45
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:12,391
Here is Revoke Line's recorded incident response on Flux Nova.

46
00:03:12,391 --> 00:03:15,714
An authorized case initially receives HTTP two hundred, allow.

47
00:03:15,714 --> 00:03:20,512
A simulated provider security alert then revokes trust and increments the provider version.

48
00:03:20,512 --> 00:03:25,311
When the workflow attempts to use its old grant, the gateway returns HTTP

49
00:03:25,311 --> 00:03:30,110
four oh three, deny. The worker routes the case to a native human

50
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:33,432
review task in the B P M N engine.

51
00:03:33,432 --> 00:03:38,231
This is an actual engine task, not just a status displayed in the

52
00:03:38,231 --> 00:03:38,600
interface.

53
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:42,293
The second recorded scenario tests selective containment.

54
00:03:42,293 --> 00:03:44,945
Two independent providers are initially authorized.

55
00:03:44,945 --> 00:03:50,689
Only provider A is revoked. Its next call is denied and its workflow

56
00:03:50,689 --> 00:03:55,108
enters human review. Provider B remains authorized and completes normally.

57
00:03:55,108 --> 00:04:00,853
We verified its automated end event through Flux Nova process and activity history,

58
00:04:00,853 --> 00:04:04,388
not simply the disappearance of an active instance.

59
00:04:04,388 --> 00:04:10,133
The result demonstrates targeted containment in this two-case scenario, without unnecessarily interrupting the

60
00:04:10,133 --> 00:04:11,017
unaffected workflow.

61
00:04:11,617 --> 00:04:14,995
The third scenario tests a real service outage.

62
00:04:14,995 --> 00:04:20,485
With the same healthy provider and valid grant, the initial request is allowed.

63
00:04:20,485 --> 00:04:25,975
We stop the local Flux Nova container, and the next request returns HTTP

64
00:04:25,975 --> 00:04:31,465
five oh three, deny. After restart, the script waits for the same pinned

65
00:04:31,465 --> 00:04:33,999
policy to become available. Authorization resumes.

66
00:04:33,999 --> 00:04:36,955
Both workflow and decision services were interrupted.

67
00:04:36,955 --> 00:04:41,600
The result demonstrates fail-closed authorization and recovery, not continuous workflow availability.

68
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:46,374
The assurance view recalculates checks against saved integration evidence.

69
00:04:46,374 --> 00:04:52,402
All three recorded scenarios pass. Sixty-eight automated regression tests pass, all sixteen decision

70
00:04:52,402 --> 00:04:58,431
combinations were verified on the live engine, and strict CALM validation reports no

71
00:04:58,431 --> 00:05:04,459
errors or warnings. Production readiness is deliberately blocked because important controls remain incomplete.

72
00:05:04,459 --> 00:05:10,024
These are verifiable prototype results, with explicit boundaries, not a compliance certification.

73
00:05:10,024 --> 00:05:16,053
The code and recorded evidence are available in the official FINOS Team Kappa

74
00:05:16,053 --> 00:05:16,517
repository.

75
00:05:17,117 --> 00:05:22,857
Revoke Line delivers executable workflow and decision models, an architecture model, a runtime

76
00:05:22,857 --> 00:05:26,832
gateway, reproducible integration scripts, and an evidence assurance interface.

77
00:05:26,832 --> 00:05:32,572
Our next engineering priorities would be authenticated caller identity, encrypted transport, protected audit

78
00:05:32,572 --> 00:05:35,222
storage, and validation under concurrent workloads.

79
00:05:35,222 --> 00:05:40,521
The prototype does not revoke real external credentials or establish production readiness.

80
00:05:40,521 --> 00:05:45,820
Two contributions have been merged into the official FINOS Team Kappa repository.

81
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:51,560
The final implementation is tagged as version one point zero point zero and

82
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:54,651
is available under the Apache Two license.

83
00:05:54,651 --> 00:05:57,301
Governance should respond when trust changes.

84
00:05:57,301 --> 00:06:00,392
That is the contribution of Revoke Line.

85
00:06:00,392 --> 00:06:02,600
Thank you for your consideration.

